# publish_set_merge.list — paths that must be MERGED BY HAND, never overwritten.
# ── INPUT — hand-maintained. Nothing generates this file. ─────────────────────
#
# Used by scripts/git-utilities/publish_set.py:
#   --sync   skips these entirely and lists them at the end
#   --merge  opens meld on each one that differs, in turn
#   --diff   reports them as REVIEW rather than WOULD CHANGE
#
# Everything else in the derived closure is a straight rsync overwrite. A path
# belongs here only if the community and internal copies are legitimately allowed
# to differ — not merely because they happen to differ today.
#
# ── Assessed 2026-08-19 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The first version of this file listed every path that differed. Assessment
# showed five of those seven were not divergent at all, just a stale mirror, so
# they have been removed and will now be overwritten:
#
#   Makefile                     235 source-only lines vs 2 mirror-only, and both
#                                mirror lines are the pre-`?=` form of
#                                EHS_COMPONENT_SUPPORT_BASE / EHS_CORE_SUPPORT_BASE
#   target/platform/platform.mk  all 26 mirror-only lines are the pre-session
#                                EHS_GNU_OS_VERSION and
#                                COMPONENT_BASE_TECHNOLOGIES_OVERRIDE_PATH forms
#   configure                    2 mirror-only lines, both superseded older
#                                versions — one contains a typo ("inxwware")
#   target/envtree/              21 source-only files, ZERO mirror-only
#   target/envbuildscripts/      14 source-only files; the only 2 mirror-only are
#                                prepdeps.sh.orig and targetenv.sh.orig, which are
#                                merge leftovers and should be deleted from the
#                                mirror, not preserved
#
# The lesson: "differs" is not "diverges". Nearly all of it was the mirror being
# behind. Re-assess this file whenever an entry is added, on the same basis.

# ── Community-facing documentation ───────────────────────────────────────────

# 1 mirror-only line, and it is deliberate: the community README says the runtime
# is "published under an Open Source licence" where internal says "under a
# permissive Open Source licence". A wording choice, not staleness.
README.md

# 9 mirror-only lines documenting `make targetenv_run_tests`, the UnitTest/
# runner scripts and static analysis output. Present in the mirror, absent from
# source. Either community-specific guidance or content since removed internally
# — NOT yet established which. Merge by hand until someone decides.
DEVELOPING.md

# ── Never synced at all (listed for the record, excluded in the tool) ─────────
# TARGET.cfg          per-checkout state, not content
# COMMUNITY_RELEASE   mirror-only marker
# icons/, matrix.*    mirror-only, generated or community-specific
# *.orig              leftover merge artefacts in the mirror; should be deleted
